# Known high and critical vulnerabilities in the third-party images of docker-compose.yml that
# this repository cannot fix itself (SCF-AC-5.3, SCF-NF-6). Every entry needs a reason and expires
# at the end of a sprint; after that the container scan fails again until the image is replaced or
# the entry is renewed with a new reason.
# Renewed on 2026-11-24 (#171) until the end of Sprint 3 (2027-01-11): every image was checked with
# Trivy 0.69.3 (linux/amd64, --ignore-unfixed) against its newest tag; seaweedfs (4.55), Loki (3.7.10),
# and the collector (0.165.0) were upgraded and are clean, the entries below are those no published
# tag of the pinned version fixes (caddy:2.11-alpine of 2026-11-13, postgres:18-alpine of 2026-11-21,
# mongo:8.0 of 2026-11-20, couchdb:3.5 of 2026-11-24, grafana/tempo:2.10.10 are the newest builds;
# prometheus v3.16.0 and grafana 13.2.6 ship the same findings, node:24.22-alpine adds new ones).

# gosu in postgres:18-alpine and mongo:8.0 is built with Go 1.24.6 (stdlib); gosu only drops root
# privileges at container start and opens no network or TLS connection. gosu 1.20 is still in no
# official postgres:18 or mongo:8.0 image of 2026-11-21. Upstream must rebuild the images.
