# go-jose v4.1.4/4.1.5 (denial of service when parsing JWKs with RSA keys, fixed in 4.1.6) in the
# tempo binary of grafana/tempo:2.10.10 (newest release) and the grafana binary of grafana:13.2.5.
# Both listen only on 127.0.0.1 or the internal network and parse no JWKs from outside.
# Upstream must rebuild the images.
CVE-2026-116587 exp:2027-01-11

# npm packages bundled in node:24.14-alpine (the configuration step of the observability stack) and
# in grafana/grafana:13.2.5 (brace-expansion, minimatch, pacote, ip-address and others; the Tempo
# library in the Tempo data source). The configuration step opens no network connection; the
# dashboard tool listens only on 127.0.0.1 until TLS exists (R14). node:24.22-alpine would trade
# them for new undici findings. Upstream must update the bundled packages.
